13. The Actual Policy Being Requested

Once the ceremonial language is removed, the letter’s position is straightforward:

Do not regulate model distribution in a way that reduces the number of models being built, modified and deployed on commercial computing infrastructure.

That is a defensible lobbying position.

It is also exactly aligned with NVIDIA’s financial interests.

The company benefits when:

* closed frontier labs buy enormous training clusters;
* open-model developers train competing systems;
* universities fine-tune downloadable models;
* governments build sovereign AI infrastructure;
* companies run private deployments;
* startups benchmark dozens of alternatives;
* inference moves onto workstations and edge devices;
* and every country fears falling behind.

NVIDIA does not need one model to win.

NVIDIA needs everyone to keep racing.

That is why the letter generously concludes that society requires both closed and open frontier models.

Heads, NVIDIA sells GPUs.

Tails, NVIDIA sells GPUs.

The coin itself is available through an authorised systems partner.

