15. Final Determination

NVIDIA’s open-weights letter is presented as a principled defence of innovation, safety, competition and sovereignty.

Its practical programme is:

1. Release more models.
2. Encourage more organisations to adapt them.
3. Encourage every country to build AI infrastructure.
4. Prevent regulations that might reduce deployment.
5. Call the resulting increase in compute demand “American leadership.”
6. Sell the hardware, networking and software needed to operate it.

The letter condemns provider lock-in while NVIDIA operates the industry’s most formidable proprietary software moat.

It praises competition after regulators blocked its attempt to acquire a foundational architecture used by competing chipmakers.

It invokes sovereignty while the proposed ecosystem remains dependent on highly concentrated hardware, fabrication, networking and software supply.

It declares open weights beneficial for security without calculating whether defenders gain more than attackers.

It advocates legitimate extraction and learning from model behaviour while tightly protecting NVIDIA’s own implementations against reverse engineering and translation.

It calls for efficient specialised systems but carefully avoids asking whether many routine AI workloads should be removed from GPUs altogether.

And it promotes universal diffusion without accounting for the physical energy system required to support universal deployment.

The central contradiction can therefore be stated cleanly:

NVIDIA wants AI models open enough to proliferate, but the computing substrate closed enough to monetise every proliferation.

That is not a civilisational philosophy.

It is vertical market expansion with a bald eagle pasted onto the cover.

The future may indeed need open models.

It may need closed models.

It will certainly need competition, heterogeneous hardware, genuine portability and a serious accounting of energy and infrastructure.

What it does not need is to confuse the commercial interests of the world’s dominant accelerator supplier with the revealed moral structure of technological freedom.

NVIDIA is not handing intelligence to humanity.

It is ensuring that however humanity obtains intelligence, NVIDIA remains somewhere inside the invoice.

